# budget: large (xhigh ceiling)

Read `.pstack/compatibility.md` and `.pstack/models.json` before delegating. The version 2 JSON policy is authoritative. Run `node scripts/model-policy.mjs resolve <role>` and dispatch only a ready result. The following names refer to policy roles, not model slugs.

| Workflow roles | Resolve |
| --- | --- |
| feature, refactoring; bug-fix; perf-issue; hillclimb | `frontend-implementation` or `backend-implementation` |
| judgment and prose; how explainer; why synthesizer; reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer | `judgment` |
| hardest tasks | Scope-specific implementation and `difficult-task-review` |
| how explorer; why investigators; reflect tooling | `exploration` for reads, scope-specific implementation for edits |
| arena runners; architect runners | `judgment` for design; scope-specific implementation for code |
| arena cross-judge pool; interrogate reviewers | `frontend-review` or `backend-review`, excluding the authoring session; review in a fresh Opus session |
| swarm workers | The worker's explicit exploration, implementation, or review role |

Set the returned model and effort explicitly. Do not inherit effort, use max or higher, substitute missing providers, or run only the available members of a blocked panel. Upstream default slugs and fallback instructions do not override this policy.
